Matthew Salacain wrote:

> I'm trying to figure out how to setup the config stuff like to enable
> color and turn off autopickup by default. I'm running a linux system and
> a bash shell. Could someone let me know how I can accomplish this. I read
> the official guide and couldn't quite figure it out.
>
> Thanks!

Create a file in your home directory called .nethackrc

An example .nethackrc can be found here:
http://www.cs.sfu.ca/~bclewis/personal/stuff/dot.nethackrc

You'll want the lines
OPTIONS=color
and
OPTIONS=!autopickup
in it.

Or if you want to save space:
OPTIONS=color,!autopickup

